Z||000016||Ken Wittlief||06-13-2001||09:40 AM||||Its very easy to leave a window open on this forum, and do other work, and poke your nose back in here from time to time.<P>  not really a distraction any more that listening to the radio or a cd, or looking out the window for a few minutes, or having someone stop in your cubical for a few minutes and tell you about last nights exploits<P>  the significant difference is, if I drive in to work and my car does something funny, or if I notice something about my fiero that I want to share, there are a couple hundred other fiero owners on here that I have instant access to, and there are zero in my office at work.<P>   so sometimes, if something is on my mind about my car, i thinks its better to spew it out here, get if off my mind, and then get my energy back on my work.<P>  also I have found (maybe its only me) but sometimes when I am working on something intently, if I am distracted for a moment and do something else for a few minutes, then an idea will come to me for the thing I was working on - almost as if the idea was there all along, but my brain has to shut up for a minute so the idea can 'speak up'.<P>  this use to happen to me all the time taking finals in college. I would stew over one last question for the last ten minutes of the exam. and then when I walk out, get a can of pop or something, and start walking to my car, THEN "OH Kwrap!" then the answer would come to me.<P>  If you locked me in a cubical with no distractions for 8 hours a day - I would get less done.<P>  [Hows that for some thick rationalizing?]||||reg||1
